yPrice} → ${l.closePrice}</b></div>`
    + `<div class="t-row"><span>Leg CLV</span><b>${csgn(d.legClv,2)} pts</b></div>`;
  const w=200, off=16;
  const bw=document.getElementById('clvSvg').getBoundingClientRect().width;
  tip.style.left = (px+off+w>bw ? px-w-off : px+off)+'px';
  tip.style.top = Math.max(0,py-30)+'px';
  tip.style.opacity = 1;
}

/* ---- the footnote, split ----
   ⚠️ Three things are deliberately NOT in the drawer.
   1. "Simulated league" — a truth claim about the numbers on screen, and the demo-badge
      rule is site-wide. It is a visible strip above the plot (#clvSim), not a paragraph.
   2. The coverage counts — they ARE the sample. A drawer that hides "4 of 176 excluded"
      hides it from everyone who does not click.
   3. The entry-price caveat, in short form. The chart is displaying CLV; that CLV mixes
      one checked number with one unchecked one, and that has to be readable next to it.
      The full paragraph is still in the drawer.
   Everything static goes below, verbatim. */
function clvFootLive(){
  const c = CLV.data.coverage;
  // n per player over the whole season, for the band's range — the same counts the band
  // takes its median from, so the two cannot drift.
  const ns = CLV.players.map(p => (clvSeriesFor('all')[p]||[]).length).filter(n => n > 0).sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const band = ns.length
    ? `luck band n = ${ns[0]}${ns[ns.length-1] !== ns[0] ? '–' + ns[ns.length-1] : ''}` : '';
  return `<p class="live"><b>${c.noClose} of ${c.legs}</b> legs have no capturable close and are excluded`
    + ` · <b>${c.pushes}</b> push${c.pushes===1?'':'es'} dropped`
    + (band ? ` · ${band}` : '')
    + ` · captured entries only; self-priced legs are excluded</p>`;
}

function clvMethod(){
  // The counts appear on the live line too, and on purpose: up there they are the
  // sample, down here they are the sentence explaining what an exclusion means. Same
  // source both times, so they cannot disagree.
  const c = CLV.data.coverage;
  return `<details class="method"><summary>How this chart is built</summary><div class="method-body">`
    + `<b>How the axes are built.</b> Both prices are de-vigged proportionally against the opposite side, so a `
    + `<code>-200</code> favourite quoted with the usual hold is treated as roughly 65%, not 66.7%. `
    + `<b>x</b> = mean of <code>p_close − p_entry</code> across a player's graded legs to date, in probability `
    + `points; positive means the market moved toward their side after they bet. `
    + `<b>y</b> = <code>(wins ÷ n) − mean(p_close)</code>, also in points; the closing line sets the bar. `
    + `Pushes and voids are dropped from both. Same unit on both axes, so the quadrants are comparable.<br><br>`
    + `<b>One book, both ends.</b> Every Bozo leg has to be a real DraftKings selection that is legal in an SGP, `
    + `so DK is the book at entry <i>and</i> at close — the price you got and the price it closed at are `
    + `like-for-like rather than a cross-book artifact. Both reach us through licensed aggregators because `
    + `DraftKings has no public odds API. <b>Self-priced props and Other legs are excluded from this chart.</b><br><br>`
    + `<b>What is not on the chart.</b> ${c.noClose} of ${c.legs} legs have no capturable close and are excluded `
    + `from both axes and from <code>n</code> — never back-filled from the entry price, and still counted in the `
    + `ledger. Every leg goes on a real bet slip, so the market always existed and always closed; a gap here means `
    + `the capture could not resolve what was typed onto the right market, and each one carries the reason it `
    + `missed. “Other” legs are the exception — free text describing an arbitrary market, with nothing to match `
    + `on. ${c.pushes} push${c.pushes===1?'':'es'} are dropped too.<br><br>`
    + `<b>The luck band.</b> The shaded strip is how far from zero a perfectly-calibrated bettor drifts by chance `
    + `alone — binomial standard error <code>√(p̄(1−p̄) ÷ n)</code> on the delta, where n is the median legs per `
    + `player so far. It starts enormous and shrinks as the season runs. <b>A dot inside ±2 SE has not `
    + `demonstrated anything</b>: after a full season plus playoffs the band is still roughly ±10 points, wider `
    + `than most of the spread on this chart. The x-axis needs far less sample to mean something than the y-axis `
    + `does, which is the honest finding here and not a flaw in the picture.<br><br>`
    + `<b>Two caveats on the band itself.</b> It assumes legs are independent, and in Bozo they are not — several `
    + `players land on the same game most weeks. Positive correlation means the league-wide delta swings further `
    + `than a pooled binomial band implies, so the band is a <i>floor</i> on the noise, not a ceiling. And p̄ `
    + `varies per player: someone who always takes −400 favourites has a different standard error from someone `
    + `at −110. A pooled band is an approximation, and the right one at eight players.`
    + (CLV.data.format === 'royale'
      ? `<br><br><b>Bozo Royale changes what n means.</b> A player chopped in week 1 has one charted leg and a `
        + `delta that says nothing about them; the survivor has fourteen. Dot size already encodes that — the `
        + `band's <code>n</code> range is printed on its label for the same reason, because a median no longer `
        + `describes most of the roster.` : '')
    + `</div></details>`;
}

/* Draw the survival curves. Same colour + shape identity as the CLV chart above — a
   player is one thing on this page, not two. */
let SURV = null, survKey = '';
function paintSurvival(){
  const card = document.getElementById('survCard');
  if(!card) return;
  if(!CLV.data || CLV.data.format !== 'royale' || onHub() || view()!=='overview'){
    card.style.display='none'; return;
  }
  // ⚠️ Re-run only when the inputs actually change. This is 4,000 seasons of resampling;
  // doing it on every render would make the board crawl for no new information.
  const key = royaleAliveNames().join(',') + '#' + (CLV.data.legs||[]).length + '#' + (S.week||1);
  if(key !== survKey){ SURV = simulateRoyale(); survKey = key; }
  const R = SURV;
  if(!R || R.tooEarly){ card.style.display='none'; return; }
  card.style.display='';

  const meta = document.getElementById('survMeta');
  meta.textContent = `${R.sims.toLocaleString()} simulated seasons · ${R.players.length} alive`
    + (isDemo() ? ' · DEMO' : '');

  /* ---- the curves ---- */
  const W=960, H=380, M={t:20,r:120,b:44,l:52};
  const PW=W-M.l-M.r, PH=H-M.t-M.b;
  // Trim the horizon to where the outcome is effectively settled — 26 weeks of flat line
  // is not information, it is just a wide chart.
  let last = 1;
  for(let w=0; w<R.horizon; w++)
    if(R.players.some(p=>R.curve[p][w] > 0.005)) last = w;
  const wk0 = S.week || 1;
  const sx = w => M.l + (last ? w/last : 0) * PW;
  const sy = v => M.t + PH - v * PH;

  let s = '';
  for(const t of [0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1]){
    s += `<line x1="${M.l}" x2="${M.l+PW}" y1="${sy(t)}" y2="${sy(t)}" stroke="var(--grid)" stroke-width="1"/>`
      + `<text class="tick" x="${M.l-10}" y="${sy(t)+4}" text-anchor="end">${Math.round(t*100)}%</text>`;
  }
  const step = last > 12 ? 4 : last > 6 ? 2 : 1;
  for(let w=0; w<=last; w+=step)
    s += `<text class="tick" x="${sx(w)}" y="${M.t+PH+20}" text-anchor="middle">wk ${wk0+w}</text>`;
  s += `<text class="axtitle" x="${M.l+PW/2}" y="${H-8}" text-anchor="middle">week</text>`;
  s += `<text class="axtitle" transform="translate(15,${M.t+PH/2}) rotate(-90)" text-anchor="middle">still alive</text>`;

  const ordered = R.players.slice().sort((a,b)=>R.win[b]-R.win[a]);
  for(const p of ordered){
    const pts = R.curve[p].slice(0,last+1).map((v,w)=>`${sx(w)},${sy(v)}`).join(' ');
    s += `<polyline points="${pts}" fill="none" stroke="var(${clvId(p).cssVar})" stroke-width="2.4"
            stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.9"/>`;
    const endV = R.curve[p][last];
    s += `<g transform="translate(${sx(last)},${sy(endV)})">${clvGlyph(p, 4.6, 'stroke="var(--surface-1)" stroke-width="1.6"')}</g>`;
    s += `<text class="dotlabel" x="${sx(last)+11}" y="${sy(endV)+4}">${esc(teamOf(p))} ${(R.win[p]*100).toFixed(0)}%</text>`;
  }
  document.getElementById('survSvg').innerHTML = s;

  /* ---- the table: the two numbers people will actually argue about ---- */
  document.getElementById('survTbl').innerHTML =
    `<tbody><tr><th>Who</th><th>Chopped next week</th><th>Takes the pot</th><th>Legs resampled</th></tr>`
    + ordered.map(p=>{
        const pool = royalePool(p);
        return `<tr><td>${esc(teamOf(p))}${chute(p)}${p===(ME&&ME.name)?' <span class="me">· you</span>':''}</td>
          <td>${pct(R.nextChop[p])}</td><td>${pct(R.win[p])}</td>
          <td class="tm">${pool.length}${pool.length<3?' — thin':''}</td></tr>`;
      }).join('') + `</tbody>`;

  /* Same split as the CLV footnote. What stays visible is what changes between loads and
     what is a claim about these numbers: that they are simulated, how many seasons, and
     whether anyone on the table has too little history to be resampled honestly. The
     method — what the sim does and does not model — is the drawer.
     ⚠️ "Simulation, not a forecast" does NOT go in the drawer. It is the same class of
     claim as the CLV chart's demo strip. */
  const thin = R.players.filter(p => royalePool(p).length < 3).length;
  document.getElementById('survFoot').innerHTML =
      `<p class="live"><b>Simulation, not a forecast.</b> ${R.sims.toLocaleString()} seasons resampled from `
    + `players' own graded legs`
    + (thin ? ` · <b>${thin} of ${R.players.length}</b> ${thin===1?'has':'have'} fewer than three legs to `
        + `resample — treat those numbers as decoration` : '')
    + (R.softLegs ? ` · <b>${R.softLegs} of ${R.totalLegs}</b> resampled legs price off a self-reported entry` : '')
    + `</p>`
    + `<details class="method"><summary>How this simulation is built</summary><div class="method-body">`
    + `<b>Simulation, not a forecast.</b> ${R.sims.toLocaleString()} seasons, each week dealing every survivor `
    + `one of their own graded legs at random and re-rolling only the outcome from that leg's de-vigged closing `
    + `price. Nobody's future betting is invented — but a player is only as predictable as their history is long, `
    + `and the <i>legs resampled</i> column is how much history there is. Under three, treat their number as `
    + `decoration.<br><br>`
    + `<b>What it does not model.</b> Legs are drawn independently, and in Bozo they are not — several players `
    + `land on the same game most weeks. That correlation makes both clean weeks and bloodbaths more common than `
    + `this shows, so the middle of this chart is too smooth. Prop and “other” legs take their Worst Beat margin `
    + `from their own price, since a binary leg has none of its own.`
    + (R.buyback ? ` Re-deploys need no assumption any more: they are automatic, so the simulation does exactly `
      + `what the league does — one each, spent on the chop, never at the final two.`
      : ``)
    + (R.softLegs ? `<br><br><b>${R.softLegs} of ${R.totalLegs} resampled legs have no captured close</b>, so their `
      + `win probability comes from the entry price instead — a self-reported number. Those legs flatter whoever `
      + `entered them optimistically.` : '')
    + `</div></details>`;
}

async function clvLoad(force){
  const card = document.getElementById('clvCard');
  if(onHub()){ card.style.display='none'; return; }
  if(CLV.loading) return;
  if(CLV.lid===LID && CLV.data && !force){
    card.style.display=view()==='overview' ? '' : 'none';
    if(view()==='diagnostics') paintDiagnosticsExplorer();
    return;
  }
  CLV.loading = true;
  try{
    const j = await wGet('/bozo/clv?league='+encodeURIComponent(LID));
    CLV.data = j; CLV.lid = LID;
    CLV.series = {}; CLV.dom = {};
    CLV.players = (j.players||[]).slice().sort();
    CLV.me = ME ? ME.name : null;
    CLV.maxWeek = Math.max(1, ...j.legs.map(l=>l.week));
    CLV.sports = [...new Set(j.legs.map(l=>l.sport))].sort();
    clvBuildIdent();
    CLV.state.on = new Set(CLV.players);
    CLV.state.sel = null; CLV.state.hover = null;
    CLV.state.week = CLV.maxWeek; CLV.state.sport = 'all';

    // Nothing graded yet is a real state, not an error. Say so instead of drawing an
    // empty axis frame, which reads as "broken".
    if(!j.legs.length){ card.style.display='none'; if(view()==='diagnostics') paintDiagnosticsExplorer(); return; }
    card.style.display=view()==='overview' ? '' : 'none';

    const wk=document.getElementById('clvWeek');
    wk.max = CLV.maxWeek; wk.value = CLV.maxWeek;
    document.getElementById('clvSport').innerHTML = '<option value="all">All sports</option>'
      + CLV.sports.map(s=>`<option value="${esc(s)}">${esc(s.toUpperCase())}</option>`).join('');
    // The demo warning is a strip above the plot, not a line in the footnote — see the
    // note above clvFootLive for why it does not go in the drawer.
    document.getElementById('clvSim').style.display = CLV.data.synthetic ? '' : 'none';
    document.getElementById('clvFoot').innerHTML = clvFootLive() + clvMethod();
    clvRender();
    if(view()==='overview') paintSurvival();
    if(view()==='diagnostics') paintDiagnosticsExplorer();
  }catch(e){
    card.style.display='none';
    if(view()==='diagnostics'){
      document.getElementById('dxMeta').textContent='ledger unavailable';
      document.getElementById('dxChart').innerHTML='<div class="dash-empty">The diagnostics ledger could not be reached. Try this sheet again in a moment.</div>';
    }
  }finally{ CLV.loading=false; }
}

(function clvWireControls(){
  const seg=(a,b,onA,onB)=>{
    const A=document.getElementById(a), B=document.getElementById(b);
    if(!A||!B) return;
    A.onclick=()=>{ A.setAttribute('aria-pressed','true'); B.setAttribute('aria-pressed','false'); onA(); };
    B.onclick=()=>{ B.setAttribute('aria-pressed','true'); A.setAttribute('aria-pressed','false'); onB(); };
  };
  seg('clv-week','clv-season', ()=>{ CLV.state.mode='week'; clvRender(); },
                               ()=>{ CLV.state.mode='season'; clvRender(); });
  seg('clv-chart','clv-table',
    ()=>{ CLV.state.display='chart';
          document.getElementById('clvChartView').hidden=false;
          document.getElementById('clvTableView').hidden=true; clvRender(); },
    ()=>{ CLV.state.display='table';
          document.getElementById('clvChartView').hidden=true;
          document.getElementById('clvTableView').hidden=false; clvRender(); });
  const wk=document.getElementById('clvWeek');
  if(wk) wk.oninput = e=>{ CLV.state.week=+e.target.value; clvRender(); };
  const bd=document.getElementById('clvBand');
  if(bd) bd.onchange = e=>{ CLV.state.band=e.target.checked; clvRender(); };
  const sp=document.getElementById('clvSport');
  // ⚠️ A sport filter rebuilds the series AND the domain for that slice. "My CLV on NBA
  // vs NFL" is a real question and the answer must not be plotted on the all-sports frame.
  if(sp) sp.onchange = e=>{ CLV.state.sport=e.target.value; CLV.state.sel=null; clvRender(); };
  const pb=document.getElementById('clvPlay');
  if(pb) pb.onclick = ()=>{
    CLV.state.playing = !CLV.state.playing;
    pb.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(CLV.state.playing));
    pb.textContent = CLV.state.playing ? '❚❚' : '▶';
    clearInterval(CLV.timer);
    if(!CLV.state.playing) return;
    if(CLV.state.week >= CLV.maxWeek) CLV.state.week = 1;
    CLV.timer = setInterval(()=>{
      CLV.state.week++;
      document.getElementById('clvWeek').value = CLV.state.week;
      clvRender();
      if(CLV.state.week >= CLV.maxWeek){
        clearInterval(CLV.timer); CLV.state.playing=false;
        pb.setAttribute('aria-pressed','false'); pb.textContent='▶';
      }
    }, 620);
  };
})();

(async function init(){
  ME = loadSession();
  // Start the two deliberately public boards immediately. They must not wait behind
  // account roster or league-directory calls: those can be slow, while the ticket is
  // the point of the page. Member-only leagues still wait for /league/list to confirm
  // that this signed-in account may see them.
  const requested=new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('l');
  if(requested && /^[a-z0-9-]{2,24}$/.test(requested)) LID=requested;
  const watchedLid=LID;
  // ⚠️ Only the one public room now. The Royale demo was the other, and it is gone —
  // eager-loading a deleted league would open a watch on state that never arrives.
  const eagerPublic = LID==='main';
  if(eagerPublic) watchState();
  await Promise.all([loadRoster(), loadLeagues()]);
  // A bad or inaccessible ?l= may be normalized by loadLeagues. The interval created
  // above reads the current LID, but its EventSource was opened for the old one.
  if(!eagerPublic) watchState();
  else if(LID!==watchedLid){ if(esHandle) esHandle.close(); refresh(); }
  renderAuth();
  loadGames('nfl');
})();
</script>

